<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Kurekchay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Kurekchay Treaty · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1804-1813">Russo-Persian War (1804–1813)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Kurekchay was signed on 14 May 1805 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-khalil-khan">Ibrahim Khalil Khan</a> of the Karabakh Khanate and the Russian commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavel-tsitsianov">Pavel Tsitsianov</a>. The khan accepted Russian suzerainty, with his family keeping internal rule in return for tribute and a Russian garrison. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> recognised Russian control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a> in the Treaty of Gulistan of 1813, and the khanate was abolished in 1822.</p></div>
